<title>GREECE: GREEK AIRFORCE FLEW 684 SEARCH &amp; RESCUE MISSIONS IN 96.</title>
<headline>GREEK AIRFORCE FLEW 684 SEARCH &amp; RESCUE MISSIONS IN 96.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's airforce said 684 flights amounting to 1,426 flight hours were devoted to search and rescue missions and air transport of patients in 1996.</p>
<p>Aircraft from the 112 squadron in Elefsina including Dornier 28 and C-130 flew missions on a 24-hour basis in all weather conditions, the airforce general headquarters said in a statement.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
